All code in this project is original. It was written from a feature list made by looking at how
SafeInCloud behaves; no SafeInCloud code, artwork, icons or text are included. Algorithms follow
their public specifications: AES-GCM (NIST SP 800-38D), PBKDF2 (RFC 8018), Argon2 (RFC 9106),
BLAKE2b (RFC 7693), ChaCha20 (RFC 8439), Salsa20 (D. J. Bernstein), TOTP (RFC 6238), and the
publicly documented KeePass KDBX 3.1 / 4.x file formats.

SafeInCloud database support is implemented from the file layout for interoperability (moving your own data
between apps). SafeInCloud is a trademark of its owner; Grove Vault is not affiliated with it.

res/raw/privileged_browsers.json lists browsers allowed to make website passkey requests. It combines Google's
published privileged-apps list with the community list maintained in the Bitwarden Android project (GPL-3.0).

The only dependency of the Android app is the Android framework. The Windows app bundles an OpenJDK runtime
(Eclipse Temurin, GPLv2 with Classpath Exception; licences in runtime/legal).
